# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated client output is NOT committed.
#
# Only the generator configuration, the build scripts, and hand-written code
# are tracked. The generated surface is reproducible from spec/ and a pinned
# generator version, and committing it once staged 489 files and 89,374
# insertions in a single commit in the predecessor repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The AutoRest scaffold, EXCEPT custom/ which is hand-written.
#
# custom/ is the one directory AutoRest intends to be hand-edited, and it is
# where the credential layer lives (Connect-FgServer and the SendAsyncStep that
# carries auth). It exists nowhere else, so it must be committed.
#
# Two things keep it safe and both are easy to break:
#   1. The negation below. Without it, hand-written source is silently never
#      committed.
#   2. --clear-output-folder empties the output folder before generating.
#      Verify it spares custom/ before trusting it with the only copy of
#      anything. See pwsh/builders/ for where that flag is passed.
pwsh/src/*
!pwsh/src/custom/

# ...but custom/ still receives two GENERATED files, and the repo rule is that
# generated output is not committed. AutoRest emits <Module>.custom.psm1 (its
# own loader, which its README says not to modify) and a README describing the
# folder. Both are recreated by every run.
pwsh/src/custom/*.custom.psm1
pwsh/src/custom/README.md

# The scaffold's former output path, kept ignored deliberately. Moving the
# output path without this un-ignored a stale generation in the predecessor
# repo. Anyone passing -OutputFolder by hand can land here again.
spec/generators/out/

# Python client scaffold, same rule: generated, not committed.
python/src/*
!python/src/README.md

# Build artifacts
**/bin/
**/obj/
_module_build/
dist/
*.nupkg

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
